# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in. Restart the dev server after.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL has a working fallback. The two Supabase variables do
# not: without them the contact form still validates and still refuses to
# fake success, it shows the phone number instead, and the server logs why.
# RESEND_API_KEY is optional in a different way: without it, storage still
# works and the visitor still sees success, the business just doesn't get
# emailed about it — see the Lead notification section below.

# ── Canonical origin (SEO) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The production domain, no trailing slash, e.g. https://www.example.com
#
# Feeds every canonical URL, the Open Graph metadataBase, every URL in
# sitemap.xml, the robots.txt sitemap pointer and every schema.org @id.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET LOCALLY AND ON PREVIEW DEPLOYS. It falls back to
# https://ryan-pressure-washing.vercel.app, which is what preview builds should
# be claiming — a preview that emits production canonicals tells Google the
# preview *is* the site.
#
# Set it in Vercel on the Production environment only. That is the single change
# needed when the real domain is registered.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Lead storage (contact form → /api/leads → Supabase) ─────────────────────
#
# Project ref ikefommkvgktpjdtaxtf. The route writes to public.ryan_leads
# using the anon/publishable key — RLS on that table permits anon to INSERT
# only, so this key can add a row and nothing else, not read, edit or delete
# one. Names match what Vercel's Supabase integration provisions in
# production; the route only reads these two server-side, the NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix is just what the integration uses, not a sign this reaches the
# browser.
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ikefommkvgktpjdtaxtf.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Lead notification (contact form → /api/leads → Resend) ──────────────────
#
# Storage above is what "received" means; this is just a heads-up email on
# top of it. If this whole section is unset, a lead still lands in Supabase
# and the visitor still sees success — the business just isn't emailed.
#
# From https://resend.com/api-keys. Needs send permission only.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Defaults to a tanygrowth.com address — the domain already verified on this
# Resend account, not rayspropertywash.com. That's deliberate: this is an
# internal notification to the business owner, not a customer-facing email,
# so the from-address doesn't need to say Ray's. Verifying rayspropertywash.com
# would need Resend's paid plan (free tier allows one domain, already spent on
# tanygrowth.com). Override only if that changes.
LEADS_FROM_EMAIL=

# Where leads land. Defaults to `site.contact.email` in src/content/site.ts,
# so leave this blank unless leads should go somewhere other than the address
# published on the site.
LEADS_TO_EMAIL=
